course: dictionary
lesson: 8075
title: Reliever: a word with three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A reliever is something that eases pain or trouble. The word comes from «relieve», which means to make something hurt less or feel lighter. Context helps you pick the right meaning, so look at the words around it.
explain: «In an asthma attack, sit the person up, help them use their reliever inhaler and fetch an adult.» The clues are asthma attack and help them use it, so a reliever inhaler must be something that helps a person breathe. Swap your meaning into the sentence: it still makes sense.
explain: Pain relievers are medicines, and you should only take them when an adult gives them to you. In sport, a reliever is a player who comes on to take over from another. Read the whole sentence to know which meaning the writer means.
fact: A reliever is something that takes away or eases pain or trouble.
fact: A pain reliever is a medicine, and you should only take it when an adult gives it to you.
fact: A reliever inhaler is an inhaler that quickly helps a person with asthma breathe; it is often blue.
fact: In baseball and cricket, a reliever is a player who comes on to take over from another.
fact: Check the words around «reliever»: talk of asthma and breathing means the inhaler kind, and talk of a game means the player kind.
exercise: «In an asthma attack, sit the person up, help them use their reliever inhaler and fetch an adult.» What does reliever inhaler mean here? | *An inhaler that quickly helps a person breathe | A bag for carrying sports kit | A player who comes on to take over in a game | A cold drink for a hot day
exercise: What is a pain reliever? | A ball that bounces high | *A medicine that eases pain, given by an adult | A type of school shoe | A player who comes on to take over
exercise: In baseball and cricket, what is a reliever? | A medicine for a sore head | *A player who comes on to take over from another | Something that makes a noise | A wooden bat
test: «Children with asthma keep a reliever inhaler close, so they can use it quickly.» What does reliever inhaler mean? | A player who takes over in a match | A bag for school books | A pain-killing tablet for a headache | *An inhaler that helps a person breathe
test: The cricket coach says, «Our reliever is coming on to bowl.» What does reliever mean? | *A player who comes on to take over from another | A bat for hitting the ball | Something that eases pain | A tired player who must sit down
exam: In «if the inhaler doesn't help, an adult calls 999», who should make the call? | The coach | The reliever | The child alone | *An adult
